# AURA — Docker build context filter.
#
# Without this file the build context is ~16 GB (.venv 1.4G + .git 1.2G +
# artifacts 13G) and `docker build` stalls before it runs a single instruction.
# With it the context is ~196 MB (measured): 193 MB of served weights and
# calibration, 3 MB of source and the web UI.
#
# Rule of thumb: if `aura_cli train` / `cli ingest` can regenerate it, it does
# not belong in the image.

# --- environments & VCS ---------------------------------------------------- #
.venv/
venv/
.git/
.github/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
aura/pytest-tmp/

# --- editor / OS noise ----------------------------------------------------- #
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# --- datasets & local-only bulk -------------------------------------------- #
datasets/
demo_data/
aura/demo_data/
mimic_cxr_data/
archive.zip
structure.txt
manifest.jsonl
media/
presentation/
presentation_assets/
demo_exports/
demo_results/
audit_artifacts/

# --- secrets (never bake into a layer) ------------------------------------- #
ibm_quantum.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
.env
.env.*

# --- artifacts: runtime state (regenerated on first boot) ------------------ #
# aura.db is 110 MB of accumulated case history and is recreated empty by
# ensure_dirs(); baking it in ships stale demo cases and bloats the image.
aura/artifacts/aura.db
aura/artifacts/inference_log.jsonl
aura/artifacts/eval_watch*.log

# --- artifacts: training-only state (never read while serving) ------------- #
aura/artifacts/optimizer.pt
aura/artifacts/last_checkpoint.pt
aura/artifacts/scheduler.pt
aura/artifacts/vision_cnn.zip
aura/artifacts/tb/
aura/artifacts/tensorboard/
**/tensorboard/

# --- artifacts: superseded / backup copies --------------------------------- #
# best_model.pt IS the promoted retrain_v2 epoch-7 checkpoint, so the source
# run directories are redundant duplicates (162 MB each).
aura/artifacts/_smoke/
aura/artifacts/_smoke2/
aura/artifacts/_synthetic_fusion_backup/
aura/artifacts/retrain_v2/
aura/artifacts/retrain_v3/
# NOTE the **/ prefixes: in .dockerignore a bare `*` does not cross a `/`, so
# `*.bak` would only match files at the context root and would leave every
# backup under aura/artifacts/ in the image.
**/*.bak
**/*.bak.*
**/*.prequantumflip.bak
**/*.superseded-*

# --- artifacts: brain (NeuroMind) ------------------------------------------ #
# cache/  11 GB of standardised voxels — rebuild with `cli ingest`
# v1_broken_quality_head/  401 MB, known-bad, kept locally as evidence only
# checkpoints/  only best_brain_model.pt is served; the other two files are
#               a 90 MB optimizer/training state and a duplicate `latest`.
# embeddings/  latest.npz is the store downstream modules must not recompute;
#              the 60 per-epoch dumps are history.
aura/artifacts/brain/cache/
aura/artifacts/brain/v1_broken_quality_head/
aura/artifacts/brain/checkpoints/training_state.pt
aura/artifacts/brain/checkpoints/latest_brain_model.pt
aura/artifacts/brain/embeddings/epoch_*.npz
aura/artifacts/brain/embeddings/epoch_*.json

# --- docs (not needed at runtime; keep the image lean) --------------------- #
# Only the top-level bibles/audits — the .md evidence files under
# aura/artifacts/ (model cards, calibration + evaluation summaries) are KB-sized
# and stay, because the model-card surface cites them.
/*.md
docs/
